module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Meromorphic.DenominatorQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.QuasicoherentBaseChange

/-!
# The ideal of denominators as affine-local ideal-sheaf data

Let `X` be a scheme, `L` an invertible sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules and `s` a meromorphic section of
`L`. `AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData` presents the ideal of denominators of `s` in the
affine-local interface `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` applied to the family of ranges of the ideal
inclusion on sections over the affine opens. That constructor takes the *largest* ideal sheaf
contained in a given family, so a priori it can shrink the family: Mathlib records only
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_ofIdeals_le`. This file proves that nothing is
lost here, and deduces that the support of the resulting ideal sheaf is nowhere dense.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.map_ideal_basicOpen_of_isQuasicoherent_image`: for a quasi-coherent
  `𝒪_X`-module `N` whose sections map to those of `𝒪_X` compatibly with scalars and restriction,
  and a family of ideals cut out as the images of those maps, the ideal over a basic open of an
  affine open is generated by the ideal over that affine open.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ideal_ofIdeals_of_isQuasicoherent_image`: consequently
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` does not shrink such a family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData_ideal`: **Tag 02P0**, the affine denominator ideal. On
  every affine open the component of `AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData` is exactly the
  range of the ideal inclusion on sections there.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData_support_isNowhereDense`: **Tag 02P0**, the support of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData` is a nowhere dense subset of `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.map_range_denominatorIdealIota_le` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.le_map_range_denominatorIdealIota`: the two halves of the compatibility of
  those ranges with restriction to a basic open, for the denominator ideal specifically; the
  first holds for an arbitrary pair of nested opens, not only for a basic open.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal` says that `ofIdeals` recovers an ideal
sheaf from its own family of components, so the family of ranges is recovered as soon as it
satisfies the structure's compatibility condition
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal_basicOpen`: the ideal over `X.basicOpen f` is
the image of the ideal over the affine open. No side condition is needed, and in particular no
quasi-compactness. Contrast `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker`, whose family is a family of
kernels and whose `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker_apply` needs `QuasiCompact` precisely to know
that the largest ideal sheaf inside that family is large enough. Here the sheaf of modules
cutting the family out is already known to be quasi-coherent
(`AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal_isQuasicoherent`), from the same hypothesis `hL` the
statement carries, and quasi-coherence gives the harder half of the compatibility directly: by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ` the sections of
the ideal over `X.basicOpen f` are the localization away from `f` of its sections over the
affine open, so a power of `f` carries any one of them into the image of the restriction map;
and `f` restricts to a unit on its own basic open, so that power may be divided out again
without leaving the image ideal. The easy half is naturality of the inclusion.

The support statement is then the source's argument in the form the cokernel support
results of the library use. On the affine neighbourhood produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_isNowhereDense_denominator` the denominator `b`
belongs to the ideal and is a nonzerodivisor, so on an affine open where `b` is invertible the
ideal inclusion is surjective on sections
(`AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_denominatorIdealIota_app_of_le_basicOpen`), the component of the
ideal sheaf there is the unit ideal, and its zero locus misses every point of that open. The
union of those opens is dense because the basic open set of a nonzerodivisor on an affine open
meets every nonempty open subset, so the support is contained in the nowhere dense complement of
a dense open set. Regularity of `s` is not used, exactly as for quasi-coherence and for the
first cokernel.

Scalars are written in the `RingCat` spelling
`(Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf X.sheaf).obj.obj (op W)` wherever a scalar action on
  sections is needed,
as in the neighbouring files: the bridging `Module` instance of `PresheafOfModules` is only found
at that spelling, while the ideals themselves live over `Γ(X, W)`, so the restricted
denominator and its inverse are introduced by `let` at the former spelling and the ideal
memberships are stated at the latter.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02P0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02P1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange
open scoped nonZeroDivisors

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### The image of the sections of a quasi-coherent module is an ideal sheaf datum -/

/-- **The image ideals of a quasi-coherent module localize on basic opens.** Let `N` be a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module whose sections over each open `W` map to `Γ(X, W)` by `ιs W`,
compatibly with scalars and with restriction, and let `I W` be the ideal of `Γ(X, W)` consisting
of the values of `ιs W`. Then for an affine open `U` and `f : Γ(X, U)`, the ideal `I (D(f))` is
generated by the image of `I U` under restriction.

This is the hypothesis `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal_basicOpen` for the
family `I`, and it is the only thing standing between such a family and an ideal sheaf datum; see
`AlgebraicGeometry.ideal_ofIdeals_of_isQuasicoherent_image`. -/
theorem map_ideal_basicOpen_of_isQuasicoherent_image {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [N.IsQuasicoherent] (ιs : ∀ W : X.Opens, Γ(N, W) → Γ(X, W))
    (hsmul : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (r : Γ(X, W)) (d : Γ(N, W)), ιs W (r • d) = r * ιs W d)
    (hnat : ∀ (W W' : X.Opens) (h : W' ≤ W) (d : Γ(N, W)),
      ιs W' (N.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op d) = X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (ιs W d))
    (I : ∀ W : X.Opens, Ideal Γ(X, W))
    (hI : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (g : Γ(X, W)), g ∈ I W ↔ ∃ d : Γ(N, W), ιs W d = g)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (f : Γ(X, U)) :
    Ideal.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op).hom (I U) =
      I (X.basicOpen f) := by
  set res := (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op).hom with hres
  let _ := moduleOfLE N (X.basicOpen_le f)
  have hloc : IsLocalizedModule.Away f (restrictₗ N (X.basicOpen_le f)) :=
    isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ N hU f rfl (X.basicOpen_le f)
  have hpow : Submonoid.powers f ≤ (IsUnit.submonoid Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)).comap res := by
    rw [Submonoid.powers_le, Submonoid.mem_comap, IsUnit.mem_submonoid_iff, hres]
    exact X.toRingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen f
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun g hg => ?_) fun g hg => ?_
  · obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := (hI U g).mp hg
    refine (hI (X.basicOpen f) _).mpr
      ⟨N.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op d, ?_⟩
    rw [hnat U (X.basicOpen f) (X.basicOpen_le f) d, hd]
  · obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := (hI (X.basicOpen f) g).mp hg
    obtain ⟨⟨x, t⟩, hxt⟩ :=
      IsLocalizedModule.surj (Submonoid.powers f) (restrictₗ N (X.basicOpen_le f)) d
    have key : res (t : Γ(X, U)) * g = res (ιs U x) := by
      rw [← hd, ← hsmul (X.basicOpen f) (res (t : Γ(X, U))) d,
        ← hnat U (X.basicOpen f) (X.basicOpen_le f) x]
      exact congrArg (ιs (X.basicOpen f)) hxt
    rw [← Ideal.unit_mul_mem_iff_mem _ (hpow t.2), key]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ((hI U _).mpr ⟨x, rfl⟩)

/-- **`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` does not shrink the image ideals of a
quasi-coherent module.** Under the hypotheses of
`AlgebraicGeometry.map_ideal_basicOpen_of_isQuasicoherent_image` the family `I`, restricted to the
affine opens, already is an ideal sheaf datum, so the largest ideal sheaf datum contained in it
is `I` itself. -/
theorem ideal_ofIdeals_of_isQuasicoherent_image {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [N.IsQuasicoherent] (ιs : ∀ W : X.Opens, Γ(N, W) → Γ(X, W))
    (hsmul : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (r : Γ(X, W)) (d : Γ(N, W)), ιs W (r • d) = r * ιs W d)
    (hnat : ∀ (W W' : X.Opens) (h : W' ≤ W) (d : Γ(N, W)),
      ιs W' (N.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op d) = X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (ιs W d))
    (I : ∀ W : X.Opens, Ideal Γ(X, W))
    (hI : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (g : Γ(X, W)), g ∈ I W ↔ ∃ d : Γ(N, W), ιs W d = g)
    (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals fun V : X.affineOpens => I V.1).ideal U = I U.1 := by
  let J : X.IdealSheafData :=
    { ideal := fun V : X.affineOpens => I V.1
      map_ideal_basicOpen := fun V g =>
        map_ideal_basicOpen_of_isQuasicoherent_image N ιs hsmul hnat I hI V.2 g }
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal J]

/-! ### The denominator ideal in the affine-local interface -/

variable (X : Scheme.{u})
  (L : SheafOfModules.{u}
    (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf))
  (s : MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L)

/-- The ideals of `Γ(X, W)` cut out by the inclusion of the ideal of denominators of `s`, in the
shape `AlgebraicGeometry.ideal_ofIdeals_of_isQuasicoherent_image` consumes: membership is being a
value of the inclusion on sections. -/
theorem mem_range_denominatorIdeal_inclusion_app_iff (W : X.Opens) (g : Γ(X, W)) :
    g ∈ ((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op W)).hom.range ↔
      ∃ d : Γ(denominatorIdeal X L s, W),
        ((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op W)).hom d = g :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- Restriction carries denominators to denominators: the image of the range of the ideal
inclusion over an open set is contained in its range over a smaller one. This is naturality of
the inclusion. -/
theorem map_range_denominatorIdealIota_le {U V : X.Opens} (hVU : V ≤ U) :
    Ideal.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom
        (((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op U)).hom.range : Ideal Γ(X, U)) ≤
      (((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op V)).hom.range : Ideal Γ(X, V)) := by
  refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr ?_
  rintro x ⟨d, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨(denominatorIdeal X L s).val.restrictₛₗ (homOfLE hVU).op d,
    PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (denominatorIdealι X L s).val (homOfLE hVU).op d⟩

/-- The image of the range of the ideal inclusion over an affine open `U` under restriction to
`X.basicOpen f` is the range over `X.basicOpen f`, by quasi-coherence of the ideal of
denominators. -/
private theorem map_ideal_basicOpen_denominatorIdeal
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (f : Γ(X, U)) :
    Ideal.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op).hom
        (((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op U)).hom.range : Ideal Γ(X, U)) =
      (((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op (X.basicOpen f))).hom.range :
        Ideal Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)) :=
  have := denominatorIdeal_isQuasicoherent X L s hL
  map_ideal_basicOpen_of_isQuasicoherent_image (denominatorIdeal X L s)
    (fun W => ((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op W)).hom)
    (fun _ r d => ((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app _).hom.map_smul r d)
    (fun _ _ h d => PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (denominatorIdealι X L s).val
      (homOfLE h).op d)
    (fun W => ((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op W)).hom.range) (fun _ _ => Iff.rfl) hU f

/-- **Nothing is lost on a basic open.** The range of the ideal inclusion over `X.basicOpen f` is
contained in the image of its range over an affine open containing `X.basicOpen f`.

This is where quasi-coherence of the ideal of denominators is used: the sections of the ideal
over `X.basicOpen f` are the localization away from `f` of its sections over the affine open, so
a power of `f` carries any one of them into the image of the restriction map; and `f` restricts
to a unit on `X.basicOpen f`, so that power may be divided out again inside the image ideal. -/
theorem le_map_range_denominatorIdealIota
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (f : Γ(X, U.1)) :
    (((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op (X.basicOpen f))).hom.range :
        Ideal Γ(X, X.basicOpen f)) ≤
      Ideal.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op).hom
        (((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op U.1)).hom.range : Ideal Γ(X, U.1)) := by
  exact (map_ideal_basicOpen_denominatorIdeal X L s hL U.2 f).ge

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02P0**, the affine denominator ideal. For an invertible sheaf of
modules `L` and a meromorphic section `s` of `L`, the component of
`AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData` at an affine open `U` is exactly the range of the
inclusion of the ideal of denominators on sections over `U`: assembling the ideal sheaf from
those ranges by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` does not shrink any of
them. -/
@[stacks 02P0 "affine denominator ideal"]
theorem denominatorIdealData_ideal
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L)
    (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (denominatorIdealData X L s).ideal U =
      ((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op U.1)).hom.range :=
  let J : X.IdealSheafData :=
    { ideal := fun V => ((denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op V.1)).hom.range
      map_ideal_basicOpen := fun V g =>
        le_antisymm (map_range_denominatorIdealIota_le X L s (X.basicOpen_le g))
          (le_map_range_denominatorIdealIota X L s hL V g) }
  congrArg (fun K : X.IdealSheafData => K.ideal U)
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal J)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02P0**, the support of the ideal of denominators. For an invertible
sheaf of modules `L` and a meromorphic section `s` of `L`, the support of
`AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData` is a nowhere dense subset of `X`.

It is contained in the complement of the union, over the points of `X`, of the part of the
affine neighbourhood produced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_isNowhereDense_denominator` on which the denominator
`b` found there is invertible: on an affine open inside such a set the ideal inclusion is
surjective on sections, so by `AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealData_ideal` the component of
the ideal sheaf there is the unit ideal and its zero locus contains no point of that open. The
union is dense because the vanishing locus of a nonzerodivisor on an affine open is nowhere
dense, so its complement is nowhere dense. -/
@[stacks 02P0 "support of the denominator ideal"]
theorem denominatorIdealData_support_isNowhereDense
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj
      (Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.ringSheaf (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) X.sheaf).property
        L) :
    IsNowhereDense ((denominatorIdealData X L s).support : Set X) := by
  choose V hxV hVaff b hb hnd t ht using fun x : X =>
    exists_isAffineOpen_nhds_isNowhereDense_denominator X L hL s x
  have hcompl : IsNowhereDense
      (((⨆ y : X, (V y ⊓ X.basicOpen (b y)) : X.Opens) : Set X)ᶜ) :=
    isNowhereDense_compl_of_dense X (Opens.isOpen _) fun y => closure_mono
      (fun z hz => le_iSup (fun x : X => V x ⊓ X.basicOpen (b x)) y hz)
      (mem_closure_inf_basicOpen_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors X (hVaff y) (hb y) (hxV y))
  refine hcompl.mono fun x hx => ?_
  rw [Set.mem_compl_iff]
  intro hxZ
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.mp hxZ
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hxU, hUle⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hy (V y ⊓ X.basicOpen (b y)).2
  have hideal : (denominatorIdealData X L s).ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = ⊤ := by
    rw [denominatorIdealData_ideal X L s hL ⟨U, hU⟩]
    exact LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr <|
      surjective_denominatorIdealIota_app_of_le_basicOpen X L s (b y) (t y) (ht y)
        (show U ≤ X.basicOpen (b y) from fun z hz => (hUle hz).2)
  have hxs : x ∈ (denominatorIdealData X L s).support := hx
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem (U := ⟨U, hU⟩) hxU, hideal,
    Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff] at hxs
  exact hxs 1 (by simp) (by rwa [X.basicOpen_one])

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
